namespace DriftSharpNo

/-- Prefix sum of the window sequence: sumTo f K = f 0 + ... + f (K-1). -/
def sumTo (f : Nat → Int) : Nat → Int
  | 0 => 0
  | K + 1 => sumTo f K + f K

variable {dhat chat d1 d2 c1 c2 : Nat → Int}

/-- Definitional step equation for sumTo, for literal instantiation downstream. -/
theorem sumToStep (f : Nat → Int) (K : Nat) : sumTo f (K + 1) = sumTo f K + f K := rfl

/-- compareMono: response monotonicity of the exact coupling recursion
D * dhat(n+1) = Q * dhat n + D * chat n (D = 30000000, Q = 30000). If two
response sequences are driven by source sequences satisfying c1 n ≤ c2 n at
every window and the launches satisfy d1 0 ≤ d2 0, then the entire response
trajectories and their prefix sums are pointwise ordered, window by window.
This is the comparison principle that lifts any minimal-trajectory certificate
to ordinally larger admissible trajectories: dominance at the source level is
inherited exactly by the 1000:1 damped response with its 1000/999 feedback. -/
theorem compareMono
    (h1 : ∀ n, 30000000 * d1 (n + 1) = 30000 * d1 n + 30000000 * c1 n)
    (h2 : ∀ n, 30000000 * d2 (n + 1) = 30000 * d2 n + 30000000 * c2 n)
    (hc : ∀ n, c1 n ≤ c2 n) (hd : d1 0 ≤ d2 0) (K : Nat) :
    sumTo d1 K ≤ sumTo d2 K ∧ d1 K ≤ d2 K := by
  induction K with
  | zero =>
      have e1 : sumTo d1 0 = 0 := rfl
      have e2 : sumTo d2 0 = 0 := rfl
      omega
  | succ m ih =>
      have ihS := ih.1
      have ihP := ih.2
      have e1 : sumTo d1 (m + 1) = sumTo d1 m + d1 m := rfl
      have e2 : sumTo d2 (m + 1) = sumTo d2 m + d2 m := rfl
      have hA := h1 m
      have hB := h2 m
      have hcc := hc m
      omega
set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000000 in
/-- noSideForcedSharp1: the sharp no-side squeeze at the anchor-1 budget head 1541354. Under the exact coupling
recursion D * dhat(n+1) = Q * dhat n + D * chat n (D = 30000000, Q = 30000), with the launch at its
cap (dhat 0 ≥ 1000000), the source floor at its cap (chat 0 ≥ 39000), and the floor decaying no faster
than 11597/12500 = 0.92776 per window (equivalently D * chat(n+1) ≥ 27832800 * chat n), every
admissible response trajectory is forced above the head: sumTo dhat 93 ≥ 1541355. The certificate is the
positive-coefficient weighted identity 999 * 1000^(K-1) * sumTo dhat K = (1000^K - 1) * dhat 0 +
sum_j chat j * (1000^K - 1000^(j+1)): all coefficients are nonnegative, so no upper bound on any
quantity is needed. The ratio 11597/12500 is the Part XI arm critical point mu*_1 exactly. The integer chains: source-floor bounds chat j ≥ L_j (ceil-iterate of 11597/12500
from 39000), response potential 1000^j * dhat j ≥ XB_j, cumulative prefix bound 999 * 1000^(j-1) *
sumTo dhat j ≥ CUM_j. Consumed chain links are cleared per window so every omega call sees a
bounded sliding window of constraints. Window 93 is the certificate crossing length at the
exact ratio: the one-window slacks cert_K - (M+1) and cert_(K-1) - (M+1) straddle zero. -/
